iron statue~
The statue captures the poise of the man as he was in life. The man is less
than five and a half feet in height, but stands with feet apart and both hands
on a long wooden staff. He is dressed in fine animal furs, with a cloak of
tiger skin. His hair is long and braided with beads tied into it. His eyes
seem to glare at you fiercly and something tells you this is a man who will
bow to no one. There is some ancient writing on the pedestel upon which the
statue stands.
~
