1000 10000 0
E
orb dark crystal~
        As you peer into the orb, time seems to move with eerie slowness and
dark visions swim in your mind. You find yourself witnessing those who have
passed before you. You see endless lines of pilgrims trudging ancient dusty
paths to reach the Great Tower, despite their weariness, they come with joy in
their hearts and the name Xerxes on their lips. You cry out to warn them, but
they seem unable to hear you. For a time, all seems well with the pilgrims, it
seems they have found the paradise they have sought. There are a few, how ever
who speak out against the words of the Priest guiding the pilgrims on their
journey to spiritual enlightment, but they are whisked away and never heard
from again. The rest embark on the fabled Trials of Xerxes, designed to test
the purity of their spirit and faith in their God.
        In the first Trial you watch as the most righteous and pure of heart
are dragged down and slain by strange Shadow creatures, their souls rise
upward to be claimed by the God they foolishly thought would save them. The
wicked and those who do little to defy evil are allowed to pass unharmed.
        Next you see the survivors pass onto the secound trial. Here they pass
impassive golems that sometimes seem to ignore the pilgrims, but then suddenly
strike out with a heavy limb to crush one utterly. You sense their actions are
not random, but controlled by some sinister force to remove all but those
whose lives have been steeped in wickedness and foul deeds. These evil-doers
are ignored and pass onto the Third Trial.
        At first it seems all the pilgrims will be slain and none will pass
any further. The evil-doers run screaming through the dark pleading for the
gods of light to forgive them their evil ways and give them one last chance
to live a good life if only they will save them now. Your not to surprised to
see their prayers go unanswered, but you watch with distaste as the horrific
undead denziens of the dark slowly kill the screaming victims, many of them
dying from pure terror rather than their injuries. Then, with growing horror,
you watch as some of the pilgrims rather than fleeing the terrible undead
creatures, rejoice in the evil prescence around them. These, the most evil of
the evil, are guided through the darkness by ghastly undead escorts,
frequently participating in bringing about the grisly death of their fellows.
Dark blessings are bestowed upon them and they pass onto the Fourth Trial.
        Here, the evil priests face not the spirits of those who where once
alive, but demonic beings who have never known anything but evil supreme. The
demons do nothing to aid the priests, who aimlessly wander the mists
hopelessly looking for a way out. Many of them eventually succumb to despair
and are torn to shreds when their faith falters. Some thou, never give in.
Strong of will and evil of spirit, these ones force the demons onto their will
and eventually conquer the Trial of Despair. Your idly curious as to what
happens to them next, but you realise with a start the vision has come to an
end.
~
